    "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nPort #6427 and #6447 from `r0.7.0` to `main` so the `fw-final` image installs cuDNN Frontend from pinned commit `8924d4b41fd678ba1b98cd7f98bb78b222637573` on `feat/1.29.0-megatron`. Without the follow-up fix, the framework's dependency override replaces the explicit Git requirement with the registry wheel.\n\n## Changelog\n\n- Add the Docker-only `CUDNN_FRONTEND_GIT_REF` build argument and document it.\n- Skip cuDNN Frontend during the framework sync, install the Git requirement with `--no-config`, and fail the build if the installed distribution does not record the requested commit.\n- Preserve registry-wheel behavior when the argument is empty and base-runtime preservation when enabled.\n\n## GitHub Actions CI\n\nValidated in an isolated Linux container with Python 3.12 and `UV_NO_SYNC=1`:\n\n- `uv run python -m pytest -q --confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/docker tests/unit_tests/docker/test_preserve_base_runtime.py` — 16 passed. The directory cutoff isolates these dependency-free tests from the GPU training fixtures.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` — passed.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nA full `fw-final` image rebuild has not been run for this port.\n\n## Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n- [x] Read and followed the contributor guidelines.\n- [x] Ran the existing relevant tests; this is an exact port of the two merged changes.\n- [x] Updated the Docker build-argument documentation.\n- Optional-import guards: not applicable; no Python APIs or dependency manifests change.\n\n## Additional Information\n\nRelated to #6427 and #6447. This is separate from #6430's registry-wheel upgrade to 1.31.0: the default Git install takes precedence in `fw-final`; an empty `CUDNN_FRONTEND_GIT_REF` keeps registry behavior.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
